# Line endings are LF for TEXT, everywhere, on every OS.
#
# Not a style preference: this repo COMMITS generated text (`src/chat/view-css.ts` is the
# stylesheet JSON-encoded, `media/view.js` is a bundle) and pins it against its source with
# `expect(VIEW_CSS).toBe(readFileSync("media/view.css"))`. With the Git-for-Windows default
# (`core.autocrlf=true`) the checkout got CRLF while the committed module kept LF, so that test
# failed on Windows only — and `prettier --check` (default `endOfLine: "lf"`) failed with it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalises in the repo AND writes LF in the working tree, so the two can
# never disagree again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.vsix binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
